RAWYING [address]
  Whatever the server answers, unprocessed, as MON's hex view: the
  status line, the headers, then the body - offset, 16 bytes in hex
  and as text a row; the first 1.25K. The address is asked for as
  given (nothing added), and a redirect isn't followed: the 3xx is
  shown. In MON's window (RAWYANG: the whole screen).
  address: http://host[:port]/path?parameters (the network first:
  NET M4), or a file - A:NAME.EXT, NAME.8BM - its bytes. None:
  HOME.8BM (this drive, else A:, else Z:). A tab: RAWYING in another
  slot. Keys: as YING's (HELP YING).
